// The UAX #29 break classes, covering.  The two value bytes hold
// Grapheme_Cluster_Break in bits 0..4, Word_Break in bits 5..9,
// Extended_Pictographic in bit 10 and Indic_Conjunct_Break in bits
// 11..12 — the declaration order of `ugrapheme`'s own tables in each
// case.  One table rather than four because the four properties change
// at nearly the same codepoints, so four tables would cost four searches
